From cee78c8e4730e8235ac3cccf79c5c73a282be612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pascal Garber <pascal@artandcode.studio>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:24:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] ipa: simple: Add a grid-only LSC algorithm

Upstream builds its LSC algorithm on libipa's LscAlgorithm, which
needs about two dozen libipa and rkisp1 commits. Instead of
backporting that chain, add a self-contained Lsc algorithm that reads
the same tuning format ("Lsc: sets: - ct, r, g, b", type "table",
17x17 grids of UQ<2, 6> values, 64 = 1.0) and interpolates between
the sets by colour temperature, updating the table only on changes of
100 K or more. LensShadingCorrectionEnable switches it off, which
passes the identity table to the debayer. Polynomial grids are not
supported.

The design and the way the table reaches the shader follow the
upstream work by Xander Pronk, Rick ten Wolde and Milan Zamazal.

Add identityLscLut to DebayerParams (from upstream 18b1542) and a
test that loads two sets through the algorithm and checks the
identity, the interpolation, the clamping, the 100 K threshold and
the disable control.

Assisted-by: AI coding agent
